  (RUNTIME-EXCEPTION.md).
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Console.pcpp - the program's console: `import Console;` adds text and VT
  escape sequences on standard output and the keyboard on standard input:
  WriteLn("{} of {}", 3, 10).

  Console writes to the program's standard output: formatted Write /
  WriteLn (as FormatStr), the cursor (0-based positions, moves, save /
  restore, hide / show), clearing, scrolling, inserting / deleting lines,
  bold and colours (the 16 standard ones, the 256-colour palette or any
  24-bit Rgb), the title and the terminal's size; text padded / aligned by
  display columns (wide characters count 2), rules, a progress bar and a
  spinner; it reads a key, waits for one or for Enter, and pauses before a
  console that closes with the program. Text is always written; escape
  sequences only on a terminal by default (a file or a pipe gets the text
  alone; SetEscapeMode changes that). The Csi consts and routines give the
  sequences to a program that writes them itself. sfml_ext converts between
  Rgb and sf::Color (sfx::fromSf / sfx::toSf).
==============================================================================*/

module unit Console;

import
  SysUtils;

// Private: the OS calls and the byte work, this unit's own translation unit.
// The routines below wrap them; every helper is named apart from the unit's
// exported names (a body in the unit's namespace would find those first).
cpp source;

